1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
 In this video, we'll be going over the installation of the Go tool chain and Visual Studio Code.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:12,000
 The first thing you'll do is open up a web browser and navigate to go.dev.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,000
 Once the page loads, click on the download link.

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:20,000
 Under feature downloads, if you're on Windows, click on the link for Microsoft Windows,

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,000
 then click on save file.

6
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:24,000
 Save it wherever you like.

7
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:28,000
 Once the download completes, open up the installer.

8
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:32,000
 Click on next, click the checkbox and click next.

9
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:36,000
 I'm using defaults, so I just click next all the way through and then click install.

10
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:44,000
 Once the install completes, click finish.

11
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:49,000
 After clicking finish, your Go tool chain is ready to run.

12
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:54,000
 Next, we'll be installing Visual Studio Code in its extensions.

13
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:01,000
 Back in your web browser, navigate to code.visualstudio.com

14
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:05,000
 Click on the download for Windows link.

15
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:10,000
 Wait for a moment and then click on save file. Save it wherever you like.

16
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:15,000
 Once the download completes, open it up.

17
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:17,000
 You'll need to accept the agreement and click next.

18
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:22,000
 I use defaults for everything, so I just click next all the way through and then click on install.

19
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:32,000
 Once the installation is complete, make sure the launch Visual Studio Code button is checked and click on finish.

20
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:35,000
 And it may take a moment to launch the first time.

21
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:39,000
 Once Visual Studio Code loads, we're going to click on the extensions button on the left.

22
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:44,000
 We'll type in Go, and it should be the first results in our extensions and have several million downloads.

23
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:47,000
 We'll then click on the install button.

24
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:52,000
 After you click on the install button, we'll need to open up a Go file in order to finish the installation.

25
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:59,000
 To do so, we can go back to the getting started page and click on open folder and open up the course content materials that you've downloaded.

26
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:06,000
 I saved mine into my documents, so just navigate to it and click select folder and then open up any of the Go files.

27
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:13,000
 You'll have a pop-up that says install or install all. Just click on install all.

28
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:21,000
 This installation process may take a lot of time as there are a lot of tools to download and install in order to get Visual Studio Code set up for Go programming.

29
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:26,000
 Once your installation finishes, click on always update if you get a pop-up.

30
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:32,000
 And you should see in your terminal that the tools have been successfully installed and you'll have a message that indicates you're ready to go.

31
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:36,000
 Once you see that message, then everything is good to go and we can start the course.

